 "text": "Hi, how have you been? They usually are, especially if you have a good one who gets to know your needs. A basic wedding gives you space to enjoy the day, while they take care of the detail. Then plan together can help, especially if you lead while she follows. Start each meeting email with the agenda and share a document. No, it means only the day itself. You still need to sort out guests, venues, and paperwork in weeks and months. It is, if you have support. A good wedding planner can make all the difference. Then maybe she can help out at small things like birthday parties. Weddings are just one part of what she'd be doing. She'd probably enjoy it too, showing off her skills while being part of something special.",
